{"name":"Umbra Sand","hex":"#87706b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"umbra","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fully shaded inner region of a shadow cast by an opaque object.\n The area on the earth or moon experiencing the total phase of an eclipse.","The area on the earth or moon experiencing the total phase of an eclipse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/umbra"},{"term":"sand","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Rock that is ground more finely than gravel, but is not as fine as silt (more formally, see grain sizes chart), forming beaches and deserts and also used in construction.\n\n A specific grade, type, or composition of sand.\n\n A beach or other mass of sand.","A specific grade, type, or composition of sand."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a light beige colour, like that of typical sand."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sand"}],"entries":[{"title":"Umbra, penumbra and antumbra","blocks":[{"text":"The umbra, penumbra and antumbra are three distinct parts of a shadow, made by any light source after impinging on an opaque object of lesser size. In cases of equal or larger impinging objects, only an umbra and penumbra are generated. Assuming no diffraction, for a collimated beam of light, only the umbra is cast."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Diagram_of_umbra%2C_penumbra_%26_antumbra.png/330px-Diagram_of_umbra%2C_penumbra_%26_antumbra.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Umbra%2C_penumbra_and_antumbra","wikidata":"Q1068535"},{"title":"Sand","blocks":[{"text":"Sand is a granular material composed of finely divided mineral particles. Sand has various compositions but is usually defined by its grain size. Sand grains are smaller than gravel and coarser than silt. Sand can also refer to a textural class of soil or soil type; i.e., a soil containing more than 85 percent sand-sized particles by mass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Libya_4608_Idehan_Ubari_Dunes_Luca_Galuzzi_2007.jpg/330px-Libya_4608_Idehan_Ubari_Dunes_Luca_Galuzzi_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sand","wikidata":"Q34679"},{"title":"Desert sand (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Desert sand is a very light and very weakly saturated reddish yellow color which corresponds specifically to the coloration of sand. It may also be regarded as a deep tone of beige."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG/330px-Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert_sand_(color)","wikidata":"Q9303163"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Antumbra.jpg/500px-Antumbra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Antumbra.jpg/500px-Antumbra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Umbra, penumbra and antumbra formed through windows and shutters","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAntumbra.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5b/Earth_umbral_cone_%28partial%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5b/Earth_umbral_cone_%28partial%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Scale diagram of Earth's shadow, showing how the umbral cone extends beyond the orbit of the Moon (The Moon is indicated by the yellow dot.)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEarth_umbral_cone_(partial).png"},{"src